## Structured Inflation Report and Monetary Policy Report observations

`inst/extdata/mpr-forecasts.rds` contains pre-extracted official forecast
observations, classifications and source receipts. The paired manifest
records the snapshot hash. These values are derived from the Bank's report
Resources, and retain original source URLs, revision hashes and applicable
third-party provenance. They are not package-authored software and are not
relicensed by MIT. The Database OGL must not be assumed to cover report
Resources or third-party inputs. The publisher has confirmed permission to redistribute this bundled snapshot.
This does not grant a blanket licence for other uses or third-party material;
consult the [Bank's current legal terms](https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/legal)
and the exact source notices for any proposed reuse.

This forecast bundle contains structured values and provenance, without raw
report PDFs, HTML, XLS/XLSX or ZIP publications. Explicit updates use bounded
temporary source staging and remove owned bodies before releasing the writer
lock by default; source retention requires an explicit opt-in.

## Runtime-downloaded assets and other third-party material

`readboe` can retrieve Bankstats workbooks, Bank Rate files, fitted
yield-curve files, and other official release assets at runtime. Those raw
assets are not bundled in this source tree. Users must follow the terms,
attribution, and third-party restrictions stated by each relevant Bank source
page. The Bank's [yield-curve methodology and terminology
page](https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/statistics/yield-curves/terminology-and-concepts)
acknowledges underlying data providers including Bloomberg, the Gilt-Edged
Market Makers' Association, Reuters, Tradeweb, and the UK Debt Management
Office. No broader OGL or MIT grant should be inferred for those assets.

The Bank also acknowledges other institutions that provide or permit the
reprinting of material. Where a Bank resource contains third-party copyright,
rights remain with the originating organisation and reuse is subject to the
relevant third party's approval. Consult the [Bank Database
help](https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/boeapps/database/Help.asp?Highlight=Hierarchy&Travel=)
and the source page for the exact series or asset before reuse.
